    feat(WTM-149): predictive foundation — rule twins, AI explanation, forecast + risk UI
    
    Completes the Founder-approved Capability-Driven Predictive Foundation.
    
    Rule Twins (authoritative, run with no AI/network/key):
    - revenue-forecast/1 (WTM-155): weighted trailing average blended with the
      least-squares trend, seasonal factor when 12+ months exist, volatility-scaled
      band. Carries a trend-drift guard so a growing business is not mistaken for a
      seasonal trough. 92 tests, hand-computed.
    - customer-risk/1 (WTM-156): lateness vs each customer's OWN cadence + loyalty
      + monetary band; entries carry customer IDs only, never names.
    - business-alerts/1 (WTM-157): revenue/orders drop, stock, cashflow, risk share.
      An empty alert list with sufficiency=sufficient is a real answer.
    
    AI layer (WTM-158/159): reads Capability Context + Rule Twin output — no more
    flat snapshot. Numbers are COPIED from the twin, never parsed from model text;
    hostile-AI test proves a model claiming '999.999.999 ₫' changes nothing.
    Zero provider spend when the twin is insufficient. AI Runtime Boundary exists
    as a designed seam and is provably unwired (structural ratchet: no file under
    lib/ references AiToolRuntime).
    
    UI (WTM-160/161): Revenue Forecast + Customer Risk screens — production
    providers, stable test IDs, l10n keys, and an insufficient state that refuses
    to render a fabricated zero. More gains 'load 12 months of sample data'.
    
    Edge cases + privacy (WTM-162/163): real-SQLite-file suite covering month
    boundary, timezone, restart determinism, reset-sample, user/sample coexistence
    and every sufficiency threshold; privacy suite proving no PII reaches any
    prompt, twin or telemetry path (with an armed negative control).
    
    Real bug found and fixed: resetting sample data crashed with FOREIGN KEY 787
    when the user had recorded their OWN order against a sample customer — the
    pinned customer is now kept (user data wins) instead of crashing the reset.
    
    Docs: ADR-TON-016, CAPABILITY-BIBLE (6-step recipe), AI-CAPABILITY-MATRIX
    part B (8 live capabilities + the invariants under test), Testing Bible P-08,
    UI levels matrix, CURRENT-STATUS, CLAUDE.md.
    
    Evidence: flutter analyze clean · 1303/1303 tests (996 → 1303)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

